<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Usman Zaki</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1859">1859</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Usman Zaki was the first emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bida">Bida</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nupe-kingdom">Nupe</a> country of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. A son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> cleric <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallam-dendo">Mallam Dendo</a>, he became ruler of the Fulani-led Nupe state in the 1830s, was driven out by rivals and then restored with support from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gwandu-emirate">Gwandu</a> around 1856, when Bida became the capital. He died in 1859 and was succeeded by his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masaba">Masaba</a>.</p></div>
